# OPSX clickable LOC_LINK contract

Use one cross-command location format for report items that reference code:

`LOC_LINK: <repo-relative-path>:<line>`

Mandatory rules:

1. If an output item references production/test code location (finding, gap, packet item, seam, test node), that item MUST include `LOC_LINK`.
2. `LOC_LINK` must be plain `path:line` text (Cursor-clickable). Do not use `file://` as the only format.
3. Keep `PATH` (file-only) optional/additive; `PATH` alone is insufficient when code-location is known.
4. Line source priority:
   - boundary call / changed hunk line;
   - symbol definition line (`def` / `class`) as fallback.
5. If exact line is unknown after bounded lookup, emit fallback symbol line and add short note explaining fallback.
6. Self-check sections of report commands must explicitly validate `LOC_LINK` presence for all relevant items.
